 "type": "Feature Layer",
 "description": "For more information about the local government model visit \"What is the Local Government Information Model.\"Layers:Atlanta City Limits: The boundaries of the City of Atlanta as defined by our ordinance.Neighborhood: The neighborhoods of Atlanta.Key Attributes:Name: The neighborhood's current name.Old Name: The previous name of the neighborhood.NPU: The NPU which the neighborhood falls within.NPU: The 25 citizen advisory councils which make recommendations to the Mayor and City Council. An NPU is composed of multiple neighborhoods.Key Attributes:Name: The name of the NPU.Land Lot Index: A grid system unique to each county which helps to identify the location of a parcel.Key Attributes:Dist_Num: The identifier for the district.LLot_Num: The identifier for the land lot.Dist_Page: A combination of Dist_Num and LL_Num which form the full land lot index.City Council Districts: The area governed by each member of the City Council.Key Attributes:Name: The number identifier of the council district.Quadrant: The four sections of Atlanta: NE, SE, NW, SW.Key Attributes:Name: The quadrant identifier.Zip Code: The dataset contains the five-digit zip codes assigned to the Metro Atlanta region by the United States Postal Service (USPS).Key Attributes:Name: The five digit identifier for the zip code.County: Counties that surround the City of Atlanta, two of which Atlanta falls in, Dekalb and Fulton.Key Attributes:Name: The name of the county.",
